WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:03.303
This suspected Chinese spy balloon

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.337
entered U.S.

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:06.373
airspace eight days ago,

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:08.408
two Saturdays ago in Alaska.

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:09.342
Once it became clear

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:10.643
that this was not an accident,

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:11.611
why did the U.S.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:14.147
not shoot it down then?

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:14.514
Well, again,

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:16.716
the president gave instructions

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:17.751
to have it

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:18.551
handled, to have it

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:20.620
shot down in a way that was safe.

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:22.922
As you may have seen, there's reporting

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.391
now that the debris field

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:25.925
that was created by this balloon

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.360
when it was shot down

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.962
was about seven miles long.

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:29.729
And so

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:30.497
any time

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:32.499
the military is considering an operation

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:33.533
like that,

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.368
they have to consider the safety

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.170
of the American people.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.772
The president called for this

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:39.773
to be dealt with

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:41.341
in a way that

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:43.076
balanced all of the different risks.

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:44.377
That's exactly what happened.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.112
Military did a terrific job.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:47.881
From our perspective in the DOT.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.516
Of course, our main concern

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:51.217
is the safety of the national airspace.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.318
This thing was above

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:55.088
where flight operations happened.

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:57.090
And so any debris would have passed

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.892
through that national airspace.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.293
But the FAA works very closely

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:01.761
with the Pentagon in this case,

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:02.929
had to do ground stops

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:04.030
on those airports

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:05.432
on the Eastern Seaboard,

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:06.032
close off

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:06.699
some of the airspace

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:08.735
to make sure that everything was safe.

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.603
And secure during the operation.

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.605
And as you know, the operation took place

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:13.740
without any damage

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:14.374
or injury

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:17.610
to any American lives or property.

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:18.978
Obviously, that's great

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.046
that there were no Americans

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:21.281
hurt by this.

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:23.116
But is it acceptable

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:24.384
that there were eight days

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:26.553
that the spy satellites above spy

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:27.654
balloon was over

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:28.321
the United States,

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:29.389
then Canada, then again

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:30.890
over the United States

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.459
from Idaho, Montana,

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:33.693
all the way through the Carolinas

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:34.894
for day after day?

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:35.595
What is the U.S.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:36.362
has communicated?

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:37.997
It's not acceptable at all.

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:40.533
That China sent this object

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:41.534
into our airspace.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.303
But in terms of how to handle it.

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:44.437
That's something that was done

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:46.473
based on assessment of the risks,

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:49.742
making sure that there was no

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:51.544
risk that

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:52.512
outweighed the

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:54.280
risks in terms of any damage

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:54.747
that would come.

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:56.449
It was handled appropriately.

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:58.351
So you say there was a seven mile

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:01.321
debris field over the Atlantic Ocean

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.555
where it was shot down.

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:03.890
Can you tell us what,

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.425
if anything, has been able

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:06.359
to be recovered?

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:08.161
Obviously, there's a lot of interest in

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:09.996
in getting the material,

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:12.031
getting the debris and,

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:12.765
you know,

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:13.199
being able

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:14.134
to conduct intelligence

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:15.535
operations of our own

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:16.302
of the United States

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:17.770
zone against

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.839
the Chinese for this balloon.

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:21.241
I really can't add

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:22.942
anything on the tactics and the timing

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.177
and the manner of it.

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:25.011
Ultimately, of course,

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:26.212
comes to the Pentagon.

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:28.948
I'm just glad that there was no damage

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:30.350
or threat to U.S.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:31.451
aviation operations

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:33.353
and that this operation took place

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:34.154
was done

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:36.122
in a very effective, excellent way,

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:36.856
as you would expect

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.358
from the American military,

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:39.826
without any consequences

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:40.827
for Americans on the ground.

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:41.394
So obviously,

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:42.195
there are a lot of concerns

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:43.496
being expressed by senators

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:44.063
and governors.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:45.999
The balloon might have flown

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:46.699
and gathered

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:47.767
intelligence over

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.202
sensitive parts

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:50.970
of the United States infrastructure.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.672
There's Malmstrom Air Force Base

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:53.606
and nuclear ballistic

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:54.874
missile fields in Montana.

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.276
If you look at the map there,

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:57.210
Whiteman Air Force

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.411
Base in Missouri, Scott

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:59.946
Air Force Base in Illinois,

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:01.014
Fort Bragg and Camp

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:02.882
Lejeune in North Carolina,

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:04.284
is the assumption

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:05.952
that the balloon was able

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:07.820
to gather sensitive information

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:08.755
and transmit

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:10.323
it back to the Chinese government.

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:11.324
Although the U.S.

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:11.858
has stated

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:14.227
that steps were taken to prevent

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:15.461
any problems

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:17.197
in terms of intelligence collection.

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:17.931
Remember,

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:19.566
we are talking about a country

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:20.900
that has a space program.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.101
So I don't know

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:22.635
all of the ins

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:23.036
and outs

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:24.571
of what this balloon was doing or

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:25.939
what its capabilities were.

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:27.540
I do know that when the president

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.442
gave the order to have this handled,

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:30.443
the military gauged

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:32.445
the different risks and the different

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.781
benefits of different approaches,

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:36.482
made the decisions that they did

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:37.951
Brought this thing down without incident.

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:38.251
Right.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:38.918
But the presumption

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:39.419
has got to be

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:40.720
that the Chinese were able

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.021
to gather intelligence

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:43.323
hovering over the United States for day

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:43.790
after day,

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:44.390
especially over

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.892
some of these sensitive sites.

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:47.360
I'm sure there's a similar presumption

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.495
about what spy satellites do.

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:51.164
That is well outside of my lane.

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:52.565
I'm just glad that nobody was hurt

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:53.566
as this thing came down.

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:55.068
When did the Biden administration

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:58.137
first learn about this balloon, the spy

00:03:58.137 --> 00:04:00.006
balloon entering U.S.

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:01.207
airspace?

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:02.942
We're told it first did so.

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:03.710
It first entered U.S.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:04.944
airspace over Alaska

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:06.512
two Saturdays at ago.

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:08.081
Is that when the Biden administration

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:08.715
learned about it?

00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:09.849
I really can't speak to that.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:10.817
What I can speak to

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:12.285
is the great cooperation

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:13.686
we have between the FAA

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:14.320
and the Pentagon

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:14.821
to make sure

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:15.788
that when you have

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.657
a special military operation

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:18.992
like what it took to bring down

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:19.792
this balloon,

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:21.394
that it happens without any threat

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:23.029
to American lives or property.

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:24.831
Lastly, on this topic,

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:26.199
will there be consequences

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:27.333
beyond shooting it down?

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:28.468
Will the Chinese government

00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:30.203
be sanctions or sanctioned

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:31.371
or penalized in any way?

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:32.071
Well, the U.S.

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:32.639
has made clear

00:04:32.639 --> 00:04:34.807
this is an unacceptable intrusion

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:35.908
into American sovereignty.

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:37.744
And I think you can expect that

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:40.013
that any further developments

00:04:40.013 --> 00:04:41.848
will be appropriate

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:43.283
in response to what happened.

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:44.117
So President

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:46.052
Biden is going to be delivering

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:46.352
this State

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:47.920
of the Union address on Tuesday.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:48.888
He's going to have a new person

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:50.123
sitting behind him.

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:50.990
The new Republican House

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.325
Speaker, Kevin McCarthy.

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:53.326
Anything President

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:55.128
Biden wants to get done

00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:56.262
over the next two years

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:58.031
other than executive actions

00:04:58.031 --> 00:05:00.500
will have to go through Kevin McCarthy.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.135
Should we expect the president to lay out

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:03.403
a long list of things

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:05.672
that are never going to happen under

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:07.240
House Republican leadership?

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.242
Or is it going to be about ways

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:09.942
and places

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:10.610
where Republicans

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.879
and Democrats can work together, areas

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:14.747
where there are common interests?

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:16.015
Well, I'm really looking forward

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:16.983
to the State of the Union

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:18.318
because first of all,

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:19.986
there are so many accomplishments

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:20.853
to talk about.

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:22.855
And many of those accomplishments

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:24.991
happened on a bipartisan basis.

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:25.692
You remember

00:05:25.692 --> 00:05:27.927
there was a lot of almost snickering

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:30.063
when the president took office

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:31.331
saying that it would be possible

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:32.031
to deliver

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:33.399
historic infrastructure

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:35.101
legislation, historic

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:36.669
economic legislation,

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:38.538
and do it on a bipartisan basis.

00:05:38.538 --> 00:05:40.039
But that's what happened.

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:41.641
And so I think the hand continues

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:42.975
to be outstretched

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:43.843
to anyone,

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:45.645
including anyone across the aisle,

00:05:45.645 --> 00:05:46.245
who's prepared

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:47.580
to work with us to get things done.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.248
But let's talk about

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:50.683
what we have to show for that,

00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:51.751
even just in the two years

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:53.252
that the administration has been here.

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:54.420
We just saw the latest round

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.255
of job numbers that came out.

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:57.390
Record low

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:58.157
unemployment, lowest

00:05:58.157 --> 00:06:00.560
we've had in more than 50 years.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:01.561
And usually

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:03.529
when unemployment is that low,

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:04.864
inflation is going up.

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:07.066
Right now, inflation is going down

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:08.901
along with unemployment.

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:09.369
We're talking about

00:06:09.369 --> 00:06:10.203
the most jobs

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:12.071
created under any president

00:06:12.071 --> 00:06:13.306
in this period, a matter of fact.

00:06:13.306 --> 00:06:15.675
President creating more jobs in two years

00:06:15.675 --> 00:06:17.643
than you have seen typically in four.

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:18.711
And coupled

00:06:18.711 --> 00:06:19.412
with things

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:22.515
that Republicans often say that is

00:06:22.615 --> 00:06:23.349
is very important

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:25.218
to them, like deficit reduction

00:06:25.218 --> 00:06:25.985
and historic

00:06:25.985 --> 00:06:27.153
reduction of the deficit

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:28.955
to the tune of 1.7 trillion.

00:06:28.955 --> 00:06:30.156
Under this president,

00:06:30.156 --> 00:06:30.656
you look at

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:31.791
what's been done in two years

00:06:31.791 --> 00:06:32.725
and I think the president's

00:06:32.725 --> 00:06:33.960
going to be going into this State

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.061
of the Union speech

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:37.296
with a context of extraordinary

00:06:37.497 --> 00:06:39.232
historic accomplishment.

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:40.199
And with that,

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:41.768
I think is a wind at our back,

00:06:41.768 --> 00:06:43.302
even with a house

00:06:43.302 --> 00:06:44.370
that is now

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:45.338
of course, in the hands

00:06:45.338 --> 00:06:47.106
of the opposite party to say, okay,

00:06:47.106 --> 00:06:48.441
what else can we get done

00:06:48.441 --> 00:06:50.076
for the benefit of the American people,

00:06:50.076 --> 00:06:50.943
first and foremost,

00:06:50.943 --> 00:06:52.812
to keep this extraordinary

00:06:52.812 --> 00:06:54.447
economic growth going

00:06:54.447 --> 00:06:56.416
and then to deal with other priorities

00:06:56.416 --> 00:06:57.417
that matter to people,

00:06:57.417 --> 00:06:59.419
whether they are in red, blue

00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:00.787
or purple areas.

00:07:00.787 --> 00:07:02.522
So just a few days ago,

00:07:02.522 --> 00:07:04.524
the chief of staff Ron Klain,

00:07:04.524 --> 00:07:05.658
left the White House.

00:07:05.658 --> 00:07:07.427
And in his farewell remarks,

00:07:07.427 --> 00:07:09.095
he referred to President Biden

00:07:09.095 --> 00:07:11.597
running for reelection in 20, 24.

00:07:11.597 --> 00:07:14.367
He'll be 81 on election day in 2024.

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:16.369
Republicans such as Ron DeSantis

00:07:16.369 --> 00:07:17.537
and Nikki Haley

00:07:17.537 --> 00:07:18.471
are already seeming

00:07:18.471 --> 00:07:20.873
to make a generational argument.

00:07:20.873 --> 00:07:22.775
Whether that's aimed at Biden or Trump

00:07:22.775 --> 00:07:23.609
that doesn't really matter

00:07:23.609 --> 00:07:25.678
they're both in advanced years.

00:07:25.678 --> 00:07:28.281
You made a similar generational argument

00:07:28.281 --> 00:07:30.283
when you were running against Joe

00:07:30.283 --> 00:07:31.751
Biden for president yourself.

00:07:31.751 --> 00:07:33.453
Are you worried that it could work

00:07:33.453 --> 00:07:34.720
in 2024

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.722
generational arguments can be powerful

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:38.891
as you said I've used them myself.

00:07:39.192 --> 00:07:41.260
The most powerful argument of all

00:07:41.494 --> 00:07:42.428
is results

00:07:42.428 --> 00:07:43.763
and you can't argue,

00:07:43.763 --> 00:07:44.096
at least

00:07:44.096 --> 00:07:44.964
I would say

00:07:44.964 --> 00:07:46.833
you can't argue with a straight face

00:07:46.833 --> 00:07:48.067
that it isn't a good thing

00:07:48.067 --> 00:07:49.001
that we have had

00:07:49.001 --> 00:07:50.436
12 million jobs

00:07:50.436 --> 00:07:51.671
created under this president

00:07:51.671 --> 00:07:52.638
and by the way

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:54.841
a lot of the jobs are in manufacturing.

00:07:55.007 --> 00:07:56.042
As someone who grew up in

00:07:56.042 --> 00:07:57.543
the industrial Midwest.

00:07:57.543 --> 00:07:59.312
It's been so moving to see

00:07:59.312 --> 00:08:01.481
hundreds of thousands of good paying

00:08:01.481 --> 00:08:03.216
manufac lecturing jobs being created

00:08:03.216 --> 00:08:04.884
including in rural areas,

00:08:04.884 --> 00:08:06.385
small towns in places

00:08:06.385 --> 00:08:07.787
like tennessee

00:08:07.787 --> 00:08:10.356
and louisiana and georgia and indiana.

00:08:10.923 --> 00:08:12.425
The kind of growth that benefits

00:08:12.425 --> 00:08:14.327
the entire american people.

00:08:14.327 --> 00:08:15.995
And I think when you look at that,

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:16.496
when you look at

00:08:16.496 --> 00:08:18.264
what america was up against

00:08:18.264 --> 00:08:20.066
when president biden took office

00:08:20.066 --> 00:08:21.901
and what has been delivered again

00:08:21.901 --> 00:08:22.502
just in these

00:08:22.502 --> 00:08:24.303
first two years of this administration,

00:08:24.303 --> 00:08:24.770
let alone

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:25.771
what's possible

00:08:25.771 --> 00:08:26.973
as we actually start

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:28.808
entering more and more, for example,

00:08:28.808 --> 00:08:30.243
of the construction phase

00:08:30.243 --> 00:08:31.677
on the infrastructure law.

00:08:31.677 --> 00:08:32.612
And I think those results

00:08:32.612 --> 00:08:33.546
are going to continue

00:08:33.546 --> 00:08:34.313
to accumulate

00:08:34.313 --> 00:08:36.482
and people will toss whatever argument

00:08:36.749 --> 00:08:38.384
they can into the mix that they think

00:08:38.384 --> 00:08:39.919
is going to benefit them the most.

00:08:39.919 --> 00:08:41.287
But at the end of the day,

00:08:41.287 --> 00:08:42.488
you can't argue

00:08:42.488 --> 00:08:44.457
with the extraordinary accomplishments

00:08:44.457 --> 00:08:45.424
more than almost

00:08:45.424 --> 00:08:47.460
any other modern president,

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.595
the present Biden has achieved, again,

00:08:49.595 --> 00:08:51.364
under the toughest of circumstances.

00:08:51.364 --> 00:08:52.965
Speaking of the industrial Midwest.

00:08:52.965 --> 00:08:53.900
You recently moved

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:55.401
from a Republican

00:08:55.401 --> 00:08:57.236
leaning in industrial Midwest state

00:08:57.236 --> 00:08:58.070
Indiana

00:08:58.070 --> 00:08:59.238
to a Democratic leaning

00:08:59.238 --> 00:09:00.840
industrial Midwest state

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:02.241
Michigan Senator

00:09:02.241 --> 00:09:02.975
Debbie Stabenow

00:09:02.975 --> 00:09:04.810
announced that she is not going to be

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:07.346
running for reelection.

00:09:07.346 --> 00:09:09.148
You and your husband and two kids have.

00:09:09.148 --> 00:09:10.149
Residents in Michigan

00:09:10.149 --> 00:09:10.950
are you going to be seeking

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:11.918
that Senate seat?

00:09:11.918 --> 00:09:14.320
No, but I really hope you're not.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.656
I'm planning to vote in that election

00:09:16.656 --> 00:09:18.724
as a resident of Michigan.

00:09:18.724 --> 00:09:20.927
But look at the job that I have is,

00:09:20.927 --> 00:09:21.360
first of all,

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:21.661
I think

00:09:21.661 --> 00:09:23.262
the best job in the federal government

00:09:23.262 --> 00:09:24.997
can be really tough and demanding

00:09:24.997 --> 00:09:26.332
with all of the problems

00:09:26.332 --> 00:09:28.000
that the transportation system

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.268
has confronted.

00:09:29.268 --> 00:09:31.203
But also incredibly rewarding.

00:09:31.203 --> 00:09:31.804
And I'm proud

00:09:31.804 --> 00:09:33.773
to be part of an administration

00:09:33.773 --> 00:09:35.875
that is doing more on transportation

00:09:35.875 --> 00:09:37.209
than has happened in my lifetime

00:09:37.209 --> 00:09:38.044
and then some

00:09:38.044 --> 00:09:40.279
not since the Eisenhower administration

00:09:40.279 --> 00:09:41.614
have we had this much going on

00:09:41.614 --> 00:09:42.848
in terms of fixing roads

00:09:42.848 --> 00:09:44.250
and bridges in this country,

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:46.852
not since Amtrak was created.

00:09:46.852 --> 00:09:49.088
Have we done more to improve rail service

00:09:49.088 --> 00:09:49.922
in this country.

00:09:49.922 --> 00:09:52.758
This job is taking 110% of my time.

00:09:52.758 --> 00:09:54.026
And obviously I serve

00:09:54.026 --> 00:09:55.227
at the pleasure of the president.

00:09:55.227 --> 00:09:56.162
But as long as

00:09:56.162 --> 00:09:57.597
he is willing to have me continue

00:09:57.597 --> 00:09:58.230
doing this work,

00:09:58.230 --> 00:09:59.599
I'm proud to be part of this team.

